  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The General Services Administration obligated $162M in FY2027 to date. The General Services Administration recorded 35,900 awards with an average award size of $4.5K, and obligations are down 99.4% year over year. The General Services Administration's recent fiscal history shows larger annual totals: FY22 $20.6B, FY23 $23.9B, FY24 $26.5B, FY25 $23.8B, and FY26 $28.7B. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction led NAICS categories in FY2027 to date with $34.3M, followed by All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services at $18.9M and Other Computer Related Services at $17.4M. BLUESTAQ LLC is the largest vendor in FY2027 to date at $24.3M, and MATOS-GRUNLEY JOINT VENTURE follows at $21.4M. The General Services Administration awarded smaller amounts across a broad set of providers, including INSURANCE AUTO AUCTIONS, INC. $10.5M and ECS FEDERAL, LLC $10M. This snapshot covers partial current-year totals and shows a sharp drop in obligations compared with prior full fiscal years.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How have obligations changed year over year?",
        "body": "The General Services Administration obligated $162M in FY2027 to date, and obligations are down 99.4% year over year. The General Services Administration recorded much larger full-year totals in prior years: FY26 $28.7B, FY25 $23.8B, FY24 $26.5B, FY23 $23.9B, and FY22 $20.6B. The General Services Administration's FY2027 total is a partial fiscal year figure and should be read as fiscal year to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which vendors and categories dominate FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "The General Services Administration's top NAICS category in FY2027 to date is Commercial and Institutional Building Construction at $34.3M, followed by All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services $18.9M and Other Computer Related Services $17.4M. The General Services Administration's top vendors in FY2027 to date are BLUESTAQ LLC $24.3M and MATOS-GRUNLEY JOINT VENTURE $21.4M, with INSURANCE AUTO AUCTIONS, INC. $10.5M and ECS FEDERAL, LLC $10M also in the top five."
      }
    ]
  },
