      "q": "How much does General Services Administration spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The General Services Administration obligated $162M in FY2027 to date. The General Services Administration recorded 35,900 awards with an average award size of $4.5K. The General Services Administration's FY2027 figure is a partial, fiscal year to date total, and prior full fiscal years were larger: FY26 $28.7B, FY25 $23.8B, FY24 $26.5B, FY23 $23.9B, FY22 $20.6B."
